{%- comment -%}
  Casa Money — formats a price with a guaranteed space between the
  currency symbol/code and the numeric amount.

  @param amount {number} - Required. Price in cents (e.g. product.price).

  Usage:
    {% render 'casa-money', amount: product.price %}

  Why: callers write "Save {% render 'casa-money' ... %}" and the
  badge must never line-break between "Save" and the amount, in any
  of the 110 enabled currencies. Compound dollar symbols (RD$, CA$,
  US$, HK$, R$) are single tokens — a blanket '$' replace splits
  them mid-symbol ("RD $ 6,500"), so symbols glued to letters are
  never touched. Idempotent — if a space is already present, no
  double-space is produced.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture _casa_money_html -%}{{ amount | money_with_currency }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Strategy: prepend one &nbsp; so the amount glues to the preceding
  word ("Save&nbsp;RD$ 6,500.00 DOP"), and nbsp-join only
  SPACE-preceded symbols (trailing-symbol locales like
  "1 234,56 $ CAD"). The collapse rules merge the caller's own
  space with the prepended entity.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign _casa_money_html = '&nbsp;' | append: _casa_money_html -%}
{%- assign _casa_money_html = _casa_money_html
    | replace: ' $', '&nbsp;$'
    | replace: ' €', '&nbsp;€'
    | replace: ' £', '&nbsp;£'
    | replace: ' ¥', '&nbsp;¥'
    | replace: ' ₹', '&nbsp;₹'
    | replace: '&nbsp;&nbsp;', '&nbsp;'
    | replace: ' &nbsp;', '&nbsp;'
    | replace: '&nbsp; ', '&nbsp;'
    | strip
-%}{{ _casa_money_html }}